omx-clap-host (0.29.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * tests: socket_conformance_test.py carries its copyright line
  * ci: no wave-deps step: every sibling this release builds on is released
  * Makefile: the test target runs the copy checks again
  * release 0.29.0: changelog lines of the preset deadline and the pool
    helpers
  * preset_list: the scanner has nine tenths of the rpc timeout, not three
    fifths
  * release 0.29.0: the wave's changelog lines and the floors and ceilings
  * Floors and ceilings on omx-contract, omx-dsp, plugin-hostd-protocol and
    plugin-db, in every place they are declared
  * ci: the packaged host's protocol floor is read as 0.2.0 or 0.3.0
  * thread pool: the helpers follow the audio thread's scheduling
  * fuzz: the records, the patch headers and the coverage floor follow the
    preset writer
  * fuzz: the preset-round-trip mutant follows the writer's new text
  * add: a clap: uri whose path holds a space is one uri
  * omx-clap-host answers hello: it registers protocol_add_hello()
  * ci: plugin-db's header installs after the checkout
  * The pin's repository is plugin-db: every name follows
  * SPDX is the shared check's, by format
  * The pin is plugin-pin's: nothing is built from plugin-hostd
  * tests: the LV2 parity harness against mod-host stays
  * ci: the ABI job installs the omx-contract the build needs
  * tools: the adapter seam table follows the direct-call run and MIDI-out
    cursor
  * ci: PLUGIN_HOSTD_REF's comment says what the tag still provides
  * No copy of plugin-hostd-protocol's declarations comes back
  * The units table and the JSON string writer are omx-contract's
  * lv2: the adapter's control writes and MIDI-out sink are direct calls
  * release: omx-clap-core 0.29.0
  * Link pin.h consumers with what plugin-hostd.pc names
  * ci: a pull request into dedupe/all builds on its siblings' dedupe/all
  * xruns sabotage: the clock arm no longer depends on the wall clock's second
  * tsan host build links libcrypto
  * chain e2e: a chain with no member is refused by the library's arity
  * socket conformance test: the dropping stand-in serves one client at a
    time and stays poisoned
  * bench-stage: the relaxed copy carries hosted_stage_limits.h
  * ci: PKG_CONFIG_PATH may be unset where the daemon's .pc path is exported;
    the fuzz seed follows data/hosting.json
  * ci: link libcrypto in the core-in-test binaries, pin plugin-hostd
    v0.16.0, install openssl for the ABI job, pin the seam table to a
    reachable commit
  * clap_host: omx_clap_host_open_timed takes a NULL id, as
    omx_clap_host_open does
  * open_timed test: a timed open with no id opens the factory's first
    descriptor
  * socket conformance: wait untimed for the first answer before the timed
    cases
  * tests: Python's byte-code cache is not tracked
  * param contract: the fingerprint's SHA-256 is libcrypto's
  * tests: the LV2 parity harness against mod-host goes
  * tests: no mod-host verb is refused by a list of the host's own
  * omx-clap-host: mod-host's refused verbs are the protocol library's list
  * tests: plugin-hostd's verbs are read from plugin-hostd-protocol's package
  * omx-clap-host: the protocol is libplugin-hostd-protocol, and
    plugin-hostd's verbs its declaration
  * hosting: the stage's numbers are spelled once, OMX_HOSTED_STAGE_*
  * ci: the shared public-sources checks; the local copies of them go
  * adapter-seam: the table classes its ref again, and CI keeps it so
  * packaging: every package installs its licence and the short README
  * packaging: no markdown in the packages; their descriptions name
    openmixer.org
  * docs: the measurements and design notes move to openmixer.org/notes
  * clap_host_test: the delay's ids are the plugin's own, its bypass found by
    CLAP_PARAM_IS_BYPASS
  * Run the commit message and private-refs checks from FreeMixer/.github
  * ci: refuse a tracked copy of a shared check

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 09:22:58 +0000
